Zenify CPU migration cost tuning for the CACHY/EEVDF tree (ghost, eevdf).

Splits sched_migration_cost out of 0003-glitched-eevdf-additions.patch so the
ZENIFY override can be applied against the CACHY layout used by the ghost and
eevdf schedulers. The BORE scheduler restructures this region, so it uses the
companion 0003-glitched-eevdf-migration-cost-bore.patch instead.

  - sched_migration_cost: ZENIFY 250us (overrides CACHY 400us / default 500us)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -85,7 +85,9 @@
 static unsigned int normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice	= 700000ULL;
 #endif /* CONFIG_CACHY */
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_CACHY
+#ifdef CONFIG_ZENIFY
+__read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 250000UL;
+#elif defined(CONFIG_CACHY)
 __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 400000UL;
 #else
 __read_mostly unsigned int sysctl_sched_migration_cost	= 500000UL;
